            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery surgery in Australia, 1975-1976. A report by the National Heart Fundation of Australia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>273-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This is a report of a register of Australian experience in coronary artery bypass graft surgery over a 12-month period from October 1, 1974, to September 30, 1975. It provides data on results up to discharge from hospital. There were 967 patients and 58 (6%) hospital death.</AbstractText>
